Dec.20, 2019
------------
Bertrand pointed me to these models based on the Kurucz and ALTAS9 codes
from Castelli et al.
http://wwwuser.oats.inaf.it/castelli/colors/BCP/

I have downloaded the tables with the revised data and reformatted the
into the svb inpout format. Unfortunately not the full 2D in logg and
Teff is covered, so I have to limit the tables to where they make sense.
Presently i have chosen the low logg area, so starting already from
logg=0.0, however this does not go to very high temperatures so i ahd to
stop at Teff=6000K. If I need hotter temperatures I will have to give up
the low logg bins, so I might have to have two sets of tables, one for
hot and one for cool stars. I do not expect any star to need both tables
though so this seems a fairly simple fix of the problem.

Jan.8, 2020
-----------

  I have made a script for generating tables which have been linearly interpolated in
FeH. All the interpolations are done with dointerFeH.csh using the awk script
interFeH.awk. This allows for LMC and SMC use.
Note that the interpolated tables have the index i added to BCP as they are no longer
"real" ATLAS 9 outputs.
